request.description:
Register a new user. Web client receives refresh token as HttpOnly cookie authn_refresh_token. Native/mobile clients receive refresh token in JSON body.

Verified response (201):
{
  "user": {
    "id": "usr_08e90da4-9e3",
    "email": "fresh.signup@authn.local",
    "email_verified": false,
    "name": "Fresh User",
    "status": "active",
    "created_at": "2026-08-06T00:26:27Z"
  },
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
}

Missing X-Authn-Publishable-Key header.

Verified response (401):
{"error":"missing publishable API key in X-Authn-Publishable-Key header"}

Email collision. Deliberate design choice (not a gap) — matches Firebase/Clerk/Auth0 behavior.

Verified response (409):
{"error":"user with this email already exists"}

Password does not satisfy active tenant policy minimum length.

Verified response (400):
{"error":"password does not meet policy requirements","missing_criteria":["min_length"]}

Rate limit: 5 attempts / 900s per IP. Includes Retry-After header.

Verified response (429):
{"error":"too many attempts, please try again later","retry_after_seconds":889}

During Redis outage, signup is rejected (fail-CLOSED). X-Authn-Degraded-Mode: true in response header.

Verified response (503):
{"error":"rate limit service unavailable"}

Validate email verification token. Token is 24h-expiry, single-use (cleared from DB on success).

Verified response (200):
{"message":"email successfully verified","email":"verify.test@authn.local","email_verified":true}

Garbage token or already-used token returns same 400. No signal which case.

Verified response (400):
{"error":"invalid or revoked token"}

Missing ?token query parameter.

Verified response (400):
{"error":"verification token query parameter is required"}

Unknown email, already-verified, and valid unverified all return identical 200 (enumeration-safe).

Verified response (200):
{"message":"if an account exists with this email address, a verification link has been sent"}

Triggered after 3 resend attempts for the same email address in 1 hour. Includes Retry-After header. Enumeration-safe.

Verified response (429):
{"error":"too many verification email requests for this address, please try again later","retry_after_seconds":900}

Authenticate user on web. Access token in JSON body, refresh token strictly in HttpOnly cookie.

Verified response (200):
{
  "user": {
    "id": "usr_vanilla_007",
    "email": "user.vanilla@authn.local",
    "email_verified": true,
    "status": "active",
    "created_at": "2026-08-05T23:32:04Z"
  },
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1..."
}

Wrong password and non-existent email return byte-for-byte identical 401 with constant-time Argon2id execution (~190ms).

Verified response (401):
{"error":"invalid email or password"}

Rate limit: 5 attempts / 900s per IP. Escalation backoff: 15m -> 1h -> 6h -> 24h.

Verified response (429):
{"error":"too many attempts, please try again later","retry_after_seconds":889}

Missing refresh_token in body and cookie.

Verified response (400):
{"error":"refresh_token required"}

Garbage, unknown, or expired token.

Verified response (401):
{"code":"invalid_token","error":"invalid or expired refresh token"}

Replaying a rotated token after 10s grace period triggers automatic account-wide session revocation.

Verified response (401):
{"code":"session_compromised","error":"session reuse detected; all sessions revoked for security"}

Returns active user sessions with parsed device information and is_current flag.

Verified response (200):
{
  "sessions": [
    {
      "id": "ses_06599d51-82f",
      "device": { "browser": "Chrome", "os": "Windows", "device": "Desktop", "label": "Chrome on Windows" },
      "ip_address": "127.0.0.1",
      "created_at": "2026-08-06T02:27:13Z",
      "is_current": true
    }
  ]
}

Revokes a specific session belonging to the caller. Rejects cross-user IDOR attacks with 403 Forbidden.

Verified response (200):
{"message":"session revoked","session_id":"ses_06599d51-82f"}

Revokes all user sessions except the active caller's session.

Verified response (200):
{"count":2,"message":"all other sessions revoked"}

Revokes all active user sessions across all devices.

Verified response (200):
{"count":3,"message":"all sessions revoked"}

Configures and enables a social identity provider for the tenant.

Verified response (200):
{"message":"provider configured successfully","provider":"google"}

Assigns an RBAC role to a target user.

Verified response (200):
{"message":"role assigned to user successfully","role":"content_manager","user_id":"usr_vanilla_007"}

Initiates an admin impersonation session for a target user.

Verified response (200 OK):
{
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
  "expires_in": 900,
  "impersonated_user": {
    "id": "usr_vanilla_007"
  }
}

Exits active impersonation session.

Verified response (200 OK):
{"impersonated_id":"usr_vanilla_007","impersonator_id":"key_test_sk_demo123_v3","message":"impersonation session exited successfully"}

Issues a new publishable or secret API key. Enforces environment isolation.

Verified response (201 Created):
{
  "key": {
    "id": "key_1e3d11488ab3",
    "name": "Stripe Webhook Handler",
    "type": "secret"
  },
  "raw_key": "sk_test_3a22900c..."
}

Revokes an API key instantly by ID.

Verified response (200 OK):
{"id":"key_1e3d11488ab3","status":"revoked"}

Registers a new webhook endpoint. SSRF validation blocks non-HTTP schemes.

Verified response (201 Created):
{
  "id": "whe_5eb5f1be-ed3",
  "secret": "whsec_da306471..."
} A webhook endpoint has no environment of its own: one list per tenant, delivered to in full. Writing it therefore takes a live key — set liveSecretKey to one. A test key is refused 403 live_key_required.
